Feature: Typed MCP catalog of daemon RPC methods
  """
  rust/rpc/src/mcp_dispatch is generated by scripts/generate-mcp-rpc.py: one
  module per FspecService method with a deny-unknown-fields Args struct, its
  JSON schema, validation and the typed call. BUG-413/BUG-367: schema()
  returns Result and catalog::methods() returns Result<Vec<Method>,
  CatalogError>, so a schema that cannot be serialized fails catalog
  construction naming the method instead of publishing null. The fspec MCP
  frontend (rust/fspec/src/client_mcp_full.rs) propagates the error and
  rejects a non-object schema. Tests: rust/rpc/tests/mcp_coverage.rs.
  """

  Background: User Story
    As an MCP client of the fspec daemon
    I want every daemon RPC described by a correct argument schema
    So that I can call any operation and see a clear error when a schema is broken

  Scenario: Every RPC has a typed MCP mapping
    Given the FspecService trait declaration
    When the MCP method catalog is built
    Then it lists exactly the declared methods, apart from the removed methods that only keep their frozen index
    And every method's schema is a closed JSON object that rejects unknown arguments

  Scenario: A schema that fails to serialize is reported with its method
    Given a method whose argument schema fails to serialize
    When the MCP catalog attaches the method name to the failure
    Then the catalog error names the method and the serialization failure
